== CM-SIC  the SIC ball in the simplex with response effects: a drivable body on which KInf1 is false
  [ok  ] p(e3) = (1 + a_i.e3)/4 sums to 1 and has every coordinate > 0 (full support) (identity)
  [ok  ] tangency control: r = -a_1 gives p_1 = 0 (a facet point, exposable by 1 - p_1) (identity)
  [note] deduce (kernel response_eq_one_forces, KInfFoundations.lean:899): a response effect certain at a full-support state has c = 1, hence equals sum p_i = 1 on the body and is not proper; so (SEC) with response effects fails at p(e3), while the ball is drivable (ball3Drive transported along the affine embedding): KInf1 is false there  (written step, not a check)

